      "route": "/conversations/[id]",
      "motion": null,
      "microAnimations": [],
      "body": "This page is one of your conversations with your AI coach, reopened from « Coach » in the menu. It holds your messages and its replies; under each reply, a quiet line says what produced it, and « Does this answer your question? » lets you say so.\n\nWrite in the message box, always in view at the foot of the page. While the coach is replying, « Stop » interrupts its reply. A reply shows from its first line; when it is long, scroll the conversation to read it to the end. The conversation scrolls on its own, under the top bar: the fiche and the item open beside it (a section, a result) stay in place and each scrolls on its own.\n\nWhile it replies, the coach shows what it is doing: each time it looks at your Jobbbox data or prepares a proposal for you, a line says so, with what it read: « Looking at your data » followed by how many items it found (12 applications), « Opening the application » or « Opening the profile » followed by its name (Airbus · Contrôleuse de gestion), « Preparing a proposal » followed by what it is about, ticked once done; « Thinking, then writing » comes last. Its reply then appears word by word, or all at once if you asked your device for less motion. Under a reply for which it looked at your data, « The coach consulted … items in Jobbbox » opens on each, by its name as it is today, with a link to its page.\n\nTo rename or delete the conversation, open its actions (« … ») beside its name in the menu. « Clear », at the top of the page, deletes all its messages; the coach's memory stays. On a phone, it is under « … », at the top right: « Clear the conversation ».\n\nIn the Jobbbox app, on iPhone, iPad or Android, you find the same conversations under « Coach » in the menu; touch and hold one to rename it (« Rename ») or delete it (« Delete »), once you confirm. While the coach is replying, the step under way shows; with VoiceOver or TalkBack, its reply is read to you once it is finished, not word by word. « Activity » shows how much of the conversation the coach reads and the AI used. Under the message box, « Report a problem » and « Suggest an idea » open the report form.\n\nIn the app, « + », left of the message box, offers two choices. « Paste a job offer link » sends the coach the link you copied: it reads the offer as when you paste its link in a message. « Attach a CV » opens your files: choose a CV as a PDF or Word file (.docx), of 10 MB at most; a larger file or one of another format is refused before anything is sent. The CV is read as on jobbbox.ai (« Stop reading the CV » interrupts it), then what was read shows in the conversation: nothing is saved before « Create the profile », which creates the profile and opens it; you correct it afterwards with « Edit the profile ». On an iPad or an Android tablet, you can also drag a PDF, a Word file or a job offer's link from another app and drop it on the message box: it is handled the same way. A photo of a printed job posting is not possible yet."
