      "body": "A profile is a role you are aiming for: a Master CV and search criteria. You can have several, depending on your plan.\n\nThe page is a conversation with your coach. If you have a CV, drop it in the « I have a CV » card: your coach reads it and proposes a Master CV. If not, click « Answer my coach's questions », above the message box: it asks about your career, one question at a time, and you answer in the message box; allow about ten minutes.\n\nEither way, you check and correct everything in the pane that opens beside the conversation, then click « Save my profile ». Closed, the pane opens again with « Review and save », with nothing lost. Nothing is added that you did not say.\n\n« Activity », at the top of the page, shows what is happening. While your coach reads your CV, « Right now » shows each step of the reading, which you can stop. The history then groups the whole creation in a single row, « Profile creation »: the CV reading, with the model that did it and its tokens, the only step done by AI; the « Onboarding questionnaire », whose questions are written by Jobbbox, « No AI », with the number of your answers; the « Review »; then « Profile created », with version 1 of your Master CV. The same row follows you to your new profile's page, with its first ATS Score once computed. The questionnaire and the review are not kept: once the page is reloaded, the row shows only the CV reading, version 1 and the ATS Score. The « Conversation context » stays empty, « The coach has not replied yet. », until your coach's first reply in the profile's conversation."
