      "body": "Signed in, the Jobbbox extension works out a job offer's Match Score with one of your profiles, then saves it to your applications, without copying it out.\n\n1. Sign in to Jobbbox in your browser, then open a job offer's page. The extension's panel shows « Signed in as … ».\n2. Click « Analyse this offer », the button the extension adds to the page. If it does not show, open the Jobbbox extension from your browser's toolbar: if it shows « Job offer found on this page. », click its « Analyse this offer » button; otherwise, click « Capture this page ». If the Jobbbox icon is not in the toolbar, click the extensions icon, the jigsaw piece, then the pin beside Jobbbox.\n3. The extension's panel shows the offer and its Match Score, worked out with one of your profiles.\n4. To compare the offer with another of your profiles, choose it in « Profile compared with this job offer »: the score is worked out again with it.\n5. At the foot of the panel, choose the profile for this application in « Profile used for this application ». If you uploaded a CV in the panel, « A new profile, from this CV » makes it a new profile.\n6. Click « Save as an application ». The offer joins your applications, as “To apply”; « See my application » opens it in Jobbbox.\n\nA job offer saved as an application from the extension also joins « Offers to handle », in Job searches, already « Followed », with the chip « Extension », which finds it again. A job offer only analysed, without « Save as an application », does not enter it."
